=== stdout ===
The fix is in. Here's the summary:

**Root cause:** `public/_a11y-fixes.css` has a light-theme rule `[class*="card"] { background: #fff !important }` — the substring selector `*="card"` matched `.chart-card` and `.project-card` on the D15 page whenever `data-theme="light"` was active in localStorage.

**Fix:** Renamed those two CSS classes in `d15-east-coast-katong.html`:
- `.chart-card` → `.chart-panel`
- `.project-card` → `.project-tile`

These new names don't contain `"card"`, so the `!important` white override no longer fires, and the dark `#1a1c24` backgrounds hold in both themes.


